# Driving the manager API directly (e.g. from a script on the server).
# The API is on 127.0.0.1:8790 (or through nginx on the admin port, 8281).
# Every request that changes something needs the session cookie and the X-CSRF-Token
# returned by login.

### Log in
POST http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "a@g.com", "password": "123456"}

### Add a project (saved, tested with nginx -t and applied)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "id": "notes", "name": "Notes", "prefix": "/notes",
  "frontend": {"host": "127.0.0.1", "port": 8400, "path_mode": "strip"},
  "app_kind": "static_dist"
}

### Disable / enable
POST http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/projects/notes/disable
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Test connectivity (direct and through the gateway)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/projects/notes/test
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Generated config and diff against the live file
GET http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/config/preview
